Receipt to JSON Android sample

Model: Xiaomi-OCR-0 by Xiaomi (https://huggingface.co/xiaomi-research/Xiaomi-OCR-0), licensed under
Apache License 2.0. The app downloads its LiteRT-LM conversion, Xiaomi-OCR-0_int8.litertlm, from
https://huggingface.co/litert-community/Xiaomi-OCR-0 (Apache License 2.0) on first use; the file is
not part of this source tree.

app/src/main/java/com/google/ai/edge/examples/receipt_to_json/PilBicubic.kt follows the bicubic
resampling of Pillow 13.0.0 (src/libImaging/Resample.c), Copyright (c) 1997-2011 by Secret Labs AB,
Copyright (c) 1995-2011 by Fredrik Lundh and contributors, Copyright (c) 2010 by Jeffrey 'Alex'
Clark and contributors, under the MIT-CMU License (licenses/Pillow-MIT-CMU.txt). It is copied from
the math to LaTeX sample proposed in google-ai-edge/litert-samples#502
(samples/litert_lm/math_to_latex), which adapted the Pillow 12.2.0 port of the image cutout sample
proposed in google-ai-edge/litert-samples#490 (samples/litert/image_cutout/kotlin_gpu).

Pictures.kt follows the picture preparation of the model card's script, ocr_xiaomi.py
(https://github.com/john-rocky/hf-to-litertlm/blob/main/xiaomiocr_work/ocr_xiaomi.py, Apache
License 2.0), and Kie.kt writes that script's key-information-extraction prompt, which is the
prompt of the model card (https://huggingface.co/xiaomi-research/Xiaomi-OCR-0, "Task prompts").

OcrEngine.kt, Photo.kt, MemoryCheck.kt, AutoRun.kt, MainActivity.kt and the data package
(data/ModelCatalog.kt, data/ModelStore.kt, data/DownloadSafety.kt) are adapted from the math to
LaTeX sample (#502), whose data package comes from this repository's voice assistant sample
(samples/litert_lm/voice_assistant).

The example receipts app/src/main/assets/examples/* were written and drawn for this sample by
tools/make_examples.py: invented stores, items and prices, in DejaVu Sans Mono and DejaVu Sans Bold
(Bitstream Vera Fonts license, DejaVu changes in the public domain).

Gradle wrapper files retain their upstream Apache License 2.0 headers.
Component license texts and their sources are under licenses/.
